part("Part 2: The virus nobody tested for", "~5:20", [
("P2-01", "Part two. The virus nobody tested for.", "", "G part card PART 2 · THE VIRUS NOBODY TESTED FOR", "PART 2 · THE VIRUS NOBODY TESTED FOR", "", "reverse cymbal + sub drop"),
("P2-02", "Ebola isn't one virus. It's a family. The one most people have heard of is called {Zaire}. That's the strain behind the big West African epidemic, and most of Congo's past outbreaks.", "F75",
 "G family tree: EBOLA VIRUSES -> ZAIRE (lit) · SUDAN · BUNDIBUGYO · others", "ZAIRE: THE FAMOUS ONE", "REPORTED · press via Wikipedia", "deep whoosh"),
("P2-03", "On the fifteenth of May, gene sequencing named the real culprit. {Bundibugyo}. A rarer cousin, named after a district in Uganda where it was first found.", "F04 F75",
 "G family tree: BUNDIBUGYO branch lights crimson", "BUNDIBUGYO VIRUS", "REPORTED · press via Wikipedia", "sub hit"),
("P2-04", "Before this year, Bundibugyo had caused only two known outbreaks. Uganda in 2007, with {thirty-seven} deaths. And Isiro, in Congo, in 2012, with thirteen.", "F08",
 "G two-bar chart: UGANDA 2007 · 37 · ISIRO 2012 · 13", "37 DEATHS · 13 DEATHS", "REPORTED · press via Wikipedia", "chart grow"),
("P2-05", "Two small outbreaks meant there was never much money to build tools against it. And that's the problem. There is no licensed {vaccine} for Bundibugyo. And no licensed treatment.", "F07",
 "G two empty shelves labelled VACCINE · TREATMENT; NONE LICENSED stamp", "NO LICENSED VACCINE · NO TREATMENT", "VERIFIED · ECDC, 16 Nov 2026", "stamp thud"),
("P2-05b", "Think about it from a drug company's side. Two outbreaks, about {fifty} deaths between them, in remote places. There was no market. So there was no vaccine.", "F08", "G maths card: 37 + 13 = 50 DEATHS · 2 OUTBREAKS · NO MARKET", "≈ 50 DEATHS IN 2 OUTBREAKS", "REPORTED · press / ILLUSTRATION · our maths", "typewriter"),
("P2-06", "Congo had a vaccine for the last big outbreak. It's called {Ervebo}, and it was built for Zaire. Against Bundibugyo, nobody knows how well it works.", "F07 F09",
 "G vial card ERVEBO · BUILT FOR: ZAIRE; question mark over BUNDIBUGYO", "ERVEBO: BUILT FOR ZAIRE", "VERIFIED · ECDC", "paper slide"),
("P2-06b", "At first, at the end of May, the World Health Organization advised {against} using it outside of trials. Now its experts suggest using it mainly inside research rules, so every dose teaches something.", "F63", "G two-step card: 28 MAY: NOT ADVISED → NOW: RESEARCH USE", "28 MAY: NOT ADVISED · NOW: RESEARCH USE", "VERIFIED · ECDC / REPORTED · WHO via press", "paper slide"),
("P2-07", "So the world started from zero. In June, a vaccine fund called CEPI put money into three candidates: {fifty million dollars} to Moderna, eight point six million to {Oxford}, and {three point two million} to IAVI.", "F11",
 "G bars: MODERNA $50M · OXFORD $8.6M · IAVI $3.2M", "CEPI: $50M · $8.6M · $3.2M", "REPORTED · press via Wikipedia", "counter roll"),
("P2-08", "In late August, Congo began giving Ervebo to frontline workers, inside research rules. And on the twenty-third of {October}, a larger trial began in Bunia.", "F09",
 "G calendar: 27 AUG circled (frontline workers) · 23 OCT circled (TUMAINI trial)", "27 AUG · 23 OCT", "VERIFIED · ECDC", "pen scratch"),
("P2-09", "In early November, the World Health Organization approved trials of two new vaccines. Results are expected in {early 2027}.", "F10",
 "G calendar: EARLY 2027 circled with RESULTS label", "RESULTS: EARLY 2027", "REPORTED · Reuters via Al Jazeera", "pen scratch"),
("P2-09b", "There's no licensed drug either. In July, trials began of two {treatments}, remdesivir and an antibody called MBP-134. Their results aren't in yet.", "F64", "G two vials: REMDESIVIR · MBP-134; TRIAL stamp 12 JUL", "TREATMENT TRIALS · 12 JUL", "REPORTED · press via Wikipedia", "stamp"),
("P2-10", "Meanwhile, the virus does what it does. Reuters reports that Bundibugyo kills about {half} of the people it infects.", "F12 M1",
 "G gauge: ≈ 49% of confirmed cases have died", "≈ 1 IN 2 HAVE DIED", "VERIFIED · ECDC counts / ILLUSTRATION · our maths", "gauge tick"),
("P2-11", "And testing is hard. Africa's disease agency said no quick test met the World Health Organization's standard. So a {reliable} result means a proper lab, often hours away on bad roads.", "F04",
 "G chain: VILLAGE -> ROAD -> LAB -> RESULT, each link lights; a clock ticks", "NO QUICK TEST · LAB ONLY", "REPORTED · Africa CDC via Wikipedia", "tick"),
("P2-12", "Second line of the bill. A virus with {no licensed vaccine}, reaching a place where it takes days to confirm a single case.", "F07",
 "G receipt: line 2 prints 'VACCINE: NONE LICENSED'", "LINE 2 · NO VACCINE", "", "receipt printer"),
])

